the rest of your life points!

252
00:16:24,380 --> 00:16:25,597
Yes, I win!

253
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:27,960
Too bad I'm not done yet.

254
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:31,880
Now quiet down so I can complete my turn.

255
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:33,828
What are you talking about?

256
00:16:33,980 --> 00:16:36,277
Both your monsters have attacked already.

257
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:38,057
There's nothing more you can do.

258
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:39,620
I can still play this.

259
00:16:39,840 --> 00:16:41,800
Go, Berserker Soul!

260
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:44,559
What are you going to do with that?

261
00:16:44,680 --> 00:16:47,940
First, I must throw out my entire hand.

262
00:16:49,260 --> 00:16:52,837
Now I shall continue to draw
cards from my deck one by one.

263
00:16:52,920 --> 00:16:57,000
And I'm not to stop until I draw
a magic or trap card. Meanwhile,

264
00:16:57,300 --> 00:16:58,977
with each monster card I draw,

265
00:16:59,060 --> 00:17:02,217
I can attack you with a creature
from my side of the field.

266
00:17:02,300 --> 00:17:06,100
As long as that creature
has 1,500 points or less.

267
00:17:07,020 --> 00:17:08,097
1,500?

268
00:17:08,180 --> 00:17:09,260
Wait a sec.

269
00:17:14,140 --> 00:17:18,537
I may have weakened my warrior's attack
power by using his special ability,

270
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:22,140
but it was well worth the price,
for now I can destroy you.

271
00:17:23,700 --> 00:17:26,160
Yugi's been planning this all along!

272
00:17:26,760 --> 00:17:29,000
It's the beginning of the end for you!

273
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:33,580
I've drawn Queen's Knight!

274
00:17:34,680 --> 00:17:38,460
And since it's a monster,
my warrior can attack!

275
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:45,200
Now for my next card!

276
00:17:48,160 --> 00:17:50,077
Looks like you're out of luck.

277
00:17:50,160 --> 00:17:51,360
Attack again!

278
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:55,960
I draw again.

279
00:17:56,360 --> 00:17:57,560
Another monster.

280
00:17:59,380 --> 00:18:01,520
This just isn't your day.

281
00:18:06,520 --> 00:18:07,350
Breaker!

282
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:08,740
Attack him again!

283
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:17,520
Let's see. Oh, well.

284
00:18:17,660 --> 00:18:18,601
Please, Sparrow!

285
00:18:18,780 --> 00:18:19,700
No more!

286
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:21,797
Let me go!

287
00:18:21,880 --> 00:18:24,300
You can stop now. It's over.

288
00:18:24,580 --> 00:18:26,227
You've already won the duel.

289
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:28,580
The seal of Orykalkos is gone.

290
00:18:30,380 --> 00:18:32,880
We have to put an end to all this.

291
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:35,660
Taya's right.

292
00:18:36,020 --> 00:18:37,780
I have a promise to keep.

293
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:51,460
So many souls, so little time.

294
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:54,520
The great Leviathan is growing impatient.

295
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:58,320
I must supply him with the
power he needs to awaken.

296
00:18:58,600 --> 00:19:01,840
And for that, I need
the soul of the Pharaoh.

297
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:09,180
Tell me where Yugi is!

298
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:12,460
Pharaoh, it's no use. You won.

299
00:19:12,740 --> 00:19:15,680
So the seal of Oricalcos took Weevil away.

300
00:19:19,400 --> 00:19:20,230
Pharaoh?

301
00:19:36,420 --> 00:19:38,840
No, I need him alive.

302
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:44,940
You all right?

303
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:46,320
Barely.
